WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.526
Everyone felt for the button, but no one could find it.

2
00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:11.240
The button that revealed the jewels had disappeared.

3
00:00:11.241 --> 00:00:17.564
"I've had enough of this whole silly business," Lord Yalding said impatiently.

4
00:00:17.565 --> 00:00:18.875
"Give me the ring.

5
00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:21.387
Since you found it in my castle, it's mine.

6
00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.480
Let's not hear another word about magic."

7
00:00:24.481 --> 00:00:29.112
"Gerald has the ring," Mabel said miserably.

8
00:00:29.113 --> 00:00:34.984
"Well then, go get him," said Lord Yalding.

9
00:00:34.985 --> 00:00:42.525
Mabel and Jimmy went to find Gerald and Kathleen.

10
00:00:42.526 --> 00:00:45.823
The four children returned to the treasure room.

11
00:00:45.824 --> 00:00:49.723
Then Gerald tried to remove the ring from his finger.

12
00:00:49.724 --> 00:00:52.438
"I can't get it off," he said.

13
00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:55.730
"This ring has a mind of its own!"

14
00:00:55.731 --> 00:00:58.275
"I'll get it off," said Lord Yalding.

15
00:00:58.276 --> 00:01:00.666
He pulled and pulled.

16
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:05.391
But he couldn't take the ring off Gerald's finger either.

17
00:01:05.392 --> 00:01:09.739
"Soap will make your finger slippery," said Lord Yalding.

18
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.248
"The ring will slide right off."

19
00:01:12.249 --> 00:01:20.668
But the children knew that soap wouldn't help.

20
00:01:20.669 --> 00:01:25.868
"I don't understand why I can't find the button," said Mabel.

21
00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:28.448
She felt for it again as she spoke.

22
00:01:28.449 --> 00:01:32.267
And suddenly the jewels appeared!

23
00:01:32.268 --> 00:01:35.328
"Oh my!" exclaimed Lord Yalding.

24
00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:38.886
Mademoiselle exclaimed something in French.

25
00:01:38.887 --> 00:01:44.517
Both adults stepped forward to admire the jewels.

26
00:01:44.518 --> 00:01:49.986
"But why now?" asked Mabel. "Why not before?"

27
00:01:49.987 --> 00:01:54.224
"It's probably magic," said Kathleen.

28
00:01:54.225 --> 00:01:59.036
"Remember Apollo told us that the ring was the heart of the magic?"

29
00:01:59.037 --> 00:02:01.167
Mabel nodded.

30
00:02:01.168 --> 00:02:07.846
"Gerald, take away the ring for a second."

31
00:02:07.847 --> 00:02:12.381
Gerald left the room, and the button disappeared.

32
00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:17.673
When he returned, the button reappeared.

33
00:02:17.674 --> 00:02:22.331
"I think that button is very cleverly hidden," said Lord Yalding.

34
00:02:22.332 --> 00:02:25.251
"And if those jewels are real—"

35
00:02:25.252 --> 00:02:31.630
"Of course they're real!" cried Mabel.

36
00:02:31.631 --> 00:02:36.721
"I'll take the ring now," said Lord Yalding.

37
00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:42.634
After half an hour and lots of soap, the ring was still on Gerald's finger.

38
00:02:42.635 --> 00:02:47.291
Then Lord Yalding said something very impatient again.

39
00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:50.522
Gerald suddenly became angry.

40
00:02:50.523 --> 00:02:54.430
"Well, I wish it would come off," said Gerald.

41
00:02:54.431 --> 00:02:58.364
Of course the ring came off instantly.

42
00:02:58.365 --> 00:03:01.223
"Thank you," said Lord Yalding.

43
00:03:01.224 --> 00:03:05.418
And he put the ring on his own finger.

44
00:03:05.419 --> 00:03:11.231
"He probably thinks it's my fault the ring was stuck," Gerald muttered.

45
00:03:11.232 --> 00:03:15.633
The next morning Lord Yalding came to see Mademoiselle.

46
00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:21.415
He went into the sitting room and closed the door.

47
00:03:21.416 --> 00:03:26.938
Kathleen and Jimmy stayed away, but Gerald sat on the stairs.

48
00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:30.945
He couldn't hear any of the conversation in the sitting room.

49
00:03:30.946 --> 00:03:33.856
But he could see the door.

50
00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:38.366
After a while Lord Yalding came out of the sitting room.

51
00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:43.100
He looked very gloomy as he put on his straw hat.

52
00:03:43.101 --> 00:03:46.026
The sitting room door was open.

53
00:03:46.027 --> 00:03:51.107
Gerald could hear crying.

54
00:03:51.108 --> 00:03:58.328
He entered the sitting room and found Mademoiselle sobbing into a couch pillow.

55
00:03:58.329 --> 00:04:01.828
"It's all over," Mademoiselle said.

56
00:04:01.829 --> 00:04:06.299
"He won't marry me!"

57
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.566
She explained what had happened.

58
00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:16.045
Last night Lord Yalding took a walk around the castle.

59
00:04:16.046 --> 00:04:22.380
He was wearing the ring, so he saw the statues move.

60
00:04:22.381 --> 00:04:25.843
Then he wished he was a statue.

61
00:04:25.844 --> 00:04:30.741
He swam to the island and feasted with the gods.

62
00:04:30.742 --> 00:04:36.359
At dawn he wished he was back to normal.

63
00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:42.508
And he decided that he must be mad.

64
00:04:42.509 --> 00:04:48.055
"He told me a madman must not marry," said Mademoiselle.

65
00:04:48.056 --> 00:04:51.904
"Did he talk to the gods?" asked Gerald.

66
00:04:51.905 --> 00:04:58.624
"Yes, and that was the maddest of all his ideas," said Mademoiselle.

67
00:04:58.625 --> 00:05:02.266
"Hermes told him to go to some temple tomorrow night.

68
00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:05.746
He must go when the moon rises."

69
00:05:05.747 --> 00:05:08.241
"That's right," said Gerald.

70
00:05:08.242 --> 00:05:09.866
"We must all go.

71
00:05:09.867 --> 00:05:11.916
I can't explain, Mademoiselle.

72
00:05:11.917 --> 00:05:21.842
But I give you my word of honor that everything will be all right."

